 "gap": {
  "lines": [
   "src/emitter.c:283,288-289,291,293,296"
  ],
  "blockers": [
   {
    "kind": "harness_const",
    "detail": "copy_event() returns libyaml's 1-on-success, but the harness treats non-zero as failure and leaves the loop after the first event; yaml_emitter_emit() is never called"
   }
  ]
 },
 "evidence": [],
 "rationale": {
  "zh": "本次提交在 parser.c 中处理“显式 key 之后关闭 flow sequence”的情况，emitter harness 会先用 parser 产生事件再交给 emitter。但该 harness 自 2020 年创建起，就把 copy_event()（成功返回 1，沿用 libyaml 约定）的返回值判反：复制成功就 goto delete_parser。于是只解析出第一个事件就退出，yaml_emitter_emit() 一次都没被调用，本次新增的 parser 路径也到不了。harness 照常编译运行、不报错，只是静默丢掉整个 emitter 的覆盖。这一退化早于本次 diff，属于非本次引入的隐式 api 退化；维护者在 oss-fuzz d94076d68f 中改为 !copy_event()。",
  "en": "This commit handles closing a flow sequence after an explicit key in parser.c; the emitter harness parses events and feeds them to the emitter. Since its creation in 2020, however, the harness inverts the result of copy_event() (which returns 1 on success, following libyaml convention): a successful copy jumps to delete_parser. It stops after the first event, yaml_emitter_emit() is never called, and the new parser path is not reached either. The harness builds and runs without any error while silently losing all emitter coverage. The degradation predates this diff: pre-existing silent api degradation, fixed in oss-fuzz d94076d68f (!copy_event())."
 },
